WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.356 --> 00:00:03.194
- What is going to be your
field of mastery in life?

00:00:03.194 --> 00:00:05.984
And if you really want
to go to that next level,

00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:07.571
then what you have to do, is you have

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:09.336
to start to think in a different way.

00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:12.919
Successful people are
extremely persistent.

00:00:14.006 --> 00:00:16.456
They do not quit when it gets tough.

00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:18.521
The more you study people
who have been successful,

00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:20.430
the more you see what it really takes.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.263
(whooshing sound)

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.644
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:24.531
My One Word is 'believe', and I believe

00:00:24.531 --> 00:00:26.443
that you have the ability to do

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.826
something special that
can change the planet.

00:00:28.826 --> 00:00:30.108
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:30.108 --> 00:00:32.381
we're going to learn from
YouTuber, entrepreneur,

00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:34.001
and life coach Leo Gura and my take

00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:36.957
on his Top Ten Rules for Success.

00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:39.015
Rule number 10 is my personal favorite,

00:00:39.015 --> 00:00:41.716
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:41.716 --> 00:00:43.212
(whooshing sound)

00:00:43.212 --> 00:00:44.765
(slamming sound)

00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:47.932
(inspirational music)

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:52.964
(beeping)

00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:56.006
- Perhaps the most important thing is,

00:00:56.006 --> 00:00:59.447
you need to find your life
purpose as soon as possible.

00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:00.780
Life purpose is,

00:01:03.743 --> 00:01:07.178
what is going to be your
field of mastery in life?

00:01:07.178 --> 00:01:09.111
How do you want to impact the world?

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:10.879
What are you most passionate about?

00:01:10.879 --> 00:01:14.316
How do you create a career out
of your top passion in life?

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:17.888
If you can figure that out
and become definite about it,

00:01:17.888 --> 00:01:20.931
and be crystal clear about it,

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:23.834
then that's going to focus
all your energy into that,

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.296
and you're going to become a
master and an expert in that.

00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:29.339
And from this will come a lot
of your financial success.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:32.404
From this also will come
a lot of fulfillment,

00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:34.322
and a lot of satisfaction.

00:01:34.322 --> 00:01:38.424
Because, fulfillment comes
from being good at something.

00:01:38.424 --> 00:01:39.800
You're not going to be fulfilled at life

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.965
by just dabbling in bunch
of little stupid things,

00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:46.068
or working a job that you're
not really excited about.

00:01:46.068 --> 00:01:48.918
You need to position yourself
as an artist in life.

00:01:48.918 --> 00:01:50.294
What's your art form?

00:01:50.294 --> 00:01:52.024
You got to find what that is.

00:01:52.024 --> 00:01:54.389
If you have some nascent passions,

00:01:54.389 --> 00:01:57.429
some passions that are
still just starting to bud,

00:01:57.429 --> 00:01:58.262
go and,

00:02:00.218 --> 00:02:02.606
nurture those, and just
see where they take you.

00:02:02.606 --> 00:02:04.807
If you're interested
in art, go do some art.

00:02:04.807 --> 00:02:06.789
If you're interested in
music, go play some music.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:09.445
If you're interested
in starting a business,

00:02:09.445 --> 00:02:11.001
go try starting a business,

00:02:11.001 --> 00:02:13.079
and just see where that takes you.

00:02:13.079 --> 00:02:15.346
You might discover,
oh, I really love this!

00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:16.806
Or no, you know, I thought I loved it,

00:02:16.806 --> 00:02:18.829
but I actually kind of hate it.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:21.787
And those are very valuable
insights for you to have.

00:02:21.787 --> 00:02:23.797
But as you're exploring around,

00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:27.631
always keep your eye out for the choice.

00:02:27.631 --> 00:02:28.575
You got to make a choice.

00:02:28.575 --> 00:02:29.896
You got to make a
commitment and a decision

00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:32.232
as to what your life is going to be about.

00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:34.057
What are you going to be mastering?

00:02:34.057 --> 00:02:36.491
Next is, set big goals.

00:02:36.491 --> 00:02:39.249
Successful people set big goals.

00:02:39.249 --> 00:02:41.696
In fact, they set gargantuan goals.

00:02:41.696 --> 00:02:43.249
And you have to do that, too.

00:02:43.249 --> 00:02:45.035
There's a tendency to say

00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:48.315
that we want to set realistic goals.

00:02:48.315 --> 00:02:51.014
You might say, well, I'm not
going to set too ambitious

00:02:51.014 --> 00:02:54.703
of a goal, because there's a
risk that I'm going to fail.

00:02:54.703 --> 00:02:56.226
Well, instead what I'm going to do,

00:02:56.226 --> 00:02:58.874
is I'm going to focus on
a goal that's realistic,

00:02:58.874 --> 00:03:01.128
that I can attain.

00:03:01.128 --> 00:03:02.958
The problem with that kind of thinking

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:06.803
is that, a lot of times, those
realistic goals that we set

00:03:06.803 --> 00:03:10.970
are undervaluing what we can
actually do in our lives.

00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:14.419
Right? You're selling yourself short.

00:03:14.419 --> 00:03:15.825
You don't really know how much potential

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:18.685
you really have until you
set a very ambitious goal.

00:03:18.685 --> 00:03:21.439
I'm sure at one point in
your life you have done that,

00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:24.191
and you've actually been able
to meet it or even exceed it,

00:03:24.191 --> 00:03:26.649
and you felt the power of that.

00:03:26.649 --> 00:03:28.603
Setting an ambitious goal, a big goal,

00:03:28.603 --> 00:03:31.520
is a great way to super
charge your motivation.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.917
And successful people are
very passionate and motivated.

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:36.218
That's because they set
big goals for themselves.

00:03:36.218 --> 00:03:39.947
If you set a weak goal, a small goal,

00:03:39.947 --> 00:03:42.616
a realistic goal, what's going to happen,

00:03:42.616 --> 00:03:45.300
is that you're not going
to get engaged with it.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.758
You're not going to get excited enough

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:48.742
to really go out there
and take the action.

00:03:48.742 --> 00:03:50.336
And, counter-intuitively,
what might happen,

00:03:50.336 --> 00:03:52.712
is that realist goal that you set

00:03:52.712 --> 00:03:54.345
might actually be harder to accomplish

00:03:54.345 --> 00:03:56.423
than the very, very ambitious goal,

00:03:56.423 --> 00:03:59.308
because the ambitious
goal has heart to it,

00:03:59.308 --> 00:04:02.460
whereas your weak,
piddly little goal, well,

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.739
who really cares if you
accomplish it or not?

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:06.553
It's not going to have
a big impact on you.

00:04:06.553 --> 00:04:08.294
It's not going to have a
big impact on the world.

00:04:08.294 --> 00:04:11.432
So, have goals out there that are a big,

00:04:11.432 --> 00:04:15.373
that are about not just you,
but about other people too.

00:04:15.373 --> 00:04:19.017
Your best strategy and
chances of success in life,

00:04:19.017 --> 00:04:20.744
chances at fulfillment, and chances

00:04:20.744 --> 00:04:23.701
at the most people liking
you, is to be yourself.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:26.090
Because when you're yourself,
your authentic self,

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.753
your magnetic.

00:04:27.753 --> 00:04:29.450
You're attractive. People
want to be near you.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.259
Maybe not the same people that want to be

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:35.622
near your fake self right
now, so, acknowledge that.

00:04:35.622 --> 00:04:38.063
I'm not saying that you can
maintain everything in your life

00:04:38.063 --> 00:04:39.751
as it is and still be yourself.

00:04:39.751 --> 00:04:41.409
You might need to make some sacrifices.

00:04:41.409 --> 00:04:42.920
There might be some costs.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.652
Because, chances are, right
now, you've whored yourself out

00:04:44.652 --> 00:04:47.117
and now you have some social debts, right?

00:04:47.117 --> 00:04:50.210
They want to tell you to stop
caring about other people

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.101
and start being authentic,
well, you're going to come up

00:04:52.101 --> 00:04:53.518
with all sorts of reasons about why

00:04:53.518 --> 00:04:54.914
that's too costly for you.

00:04:54.914 --> 00:04:57.715
You're going to say, well, then
my boss will say something bad.

00:04:57.715 --> 00:04:59.862
My job might be in danger.

00:04:59.862 --> 00:05:01.398
My relationship might be in danger.

00:05:01.398 --> 00:05:03.801
Somebody else might be in danger.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:06.284
Well, what's more important to you?

00:05:06.284 --> 00:05:07.961
Is it more important for you to be getting

00:05:07.961 --> 00:05:10.375
those shallow things?

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:13.143
Or is it more important for
you to be self expressive?

00:05:13.143 --> 00:05:15.856
To really be yourself, to
really be fulfilled inside,

00:05:15.856 --> 00:05:18.542
and then to act on that, and
to live your life from that,

00:05:18.542 --> 00:05:20.348
and to create a business from that place,

00:05:20.348 --> 00:05:21.956
to create a career from that place,

00:05:21.956 --> 00:05:25.996
to create a nice
relationship from that place?

00:05:25.996 --> 00:05:27.829
What's more important?

00:05:29.183 --> 00:05:31.275
I mean, you can still
keep whoring yourself

00:05:31.275 --> 00:05:33.328
out if you want to, but in the end,

00:05:33.328 --> 00:05:36.797
being a whore is not a good
way to go through life.

00:05:36.797 --> 00:05:39.994
So my suggestion is to bite
the bullet on this one,

00:05:39.994 --> 00:05:42.827
and be yourself despite the costs.

00:05:44.327 --> 00:05:47.013
Our next thing is, I would say,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.180
the hard work.

00:05:49.106 --> 00:05:50.670
Hard work is really, really important

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.837
to be successful, and to
be at the top ten percent

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.268
of the population in terms of success.

00:05:58.268 --> 00:06:00.967
All those people worked their ass off.

00:06:00.967 --> 00:06:04.601
You're not going to be
successful without hard work.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:06.653
And the reason, mostly,
is not even they have

00:06:06.653 --> 00:06:09.083
to go out there and build a giant empire,

00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:13.250
or you have to amass a lot
of money, or work long hours.

00:06:14.306 --> 00:06:15.643
It's not even so much about that,

00:06:15.643 --> 00:06:17.572
it's that you need to develop yourself.

00:06:17.572 --> 00:06:21.892
Because success is not so
much an outer world state

00:06:21.892 --> 00:06:24.617
as an inner world state,
and that might sound

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:28.613
kind of hokey or New Age,
but it's very, very true.

00:06:28.613 --> 00:06:30.773
Success is grounded within you.

00:06:30.773 --> 00:06:32.213
You're not going to be able to maintain

00:06:32.213 --> 00:06:35.954
any sort of level of
success if you do not have

00:06:35.954 --> 00:06:39.708
the psychology to really
follow principles,

00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:43.039
to know how to maintain success,

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:46.604
to think strategically,
to think long term,

00:06:46.604 --> 00:06:49.816
to delay gratification,
to resist addictions.

00:06:49.816 --> 00:06:52.110
All of these factors come into play.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:55.283
So really, for me, success
is grounded in self mastery.

00:06:55.283 --> 00:06:58.306
It's understanding yourself
and building on that.

00:06:58.306 --> 00:07:01.404
Building disciplines,
building successful habits,

00:07:01.404 --> 00:07:05.284
which then move you towards
where you want to be going.

00:07:05.284 --> 00:07:07.078
There's something to this idea

00:07:07.078 --> 00:07:11.245
that there can be no problem
that is not an opportunity

00:07:12.329 --> 00:07:13.614
in your life.

00:07:13.614 --> 00:07:16.119
And I think this is what the
core of positive thinking is.

00:07:16.119 --> 00:07:19.956
It's understanding that every
problem, every challenge

00:07:19.956 --> 00:07:23.587
that you have, is
ultimately an opportunity.

00:07:23.587 --> 00:07:25.665
And this is not just wishful thinking.

00:07:25.665 --> 00:07:26.908
This is not said lightly.

00:07:26.908 --> 00:07:29.135
This is something that takes some study.

00:07:29.135 --> 00:07:31.926
This takes some study and some
contemplation to understand.

00:07:31.926 --> 00:07:33.617
It takes wisdom to really understand this.

00:07:33.617 --> 00:07:34.991
You have to have some life
experience to start to see

00:07:34.991 --> 00:07:37.379
the truth of this, the depth of it.

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:39.595
'Cause there's like a
surface level understanding,

00:07:39.595 --> 00:07:42.065
and then a much deeper
layer of understanding.

00:07:42.065 --> 00:07:43.254
That's why you have to
kind of go back and look

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:46.724
at your own history, to try
to prove it to yourself.

00:07:46.724 --> 00:07:48.975
To prove yourself that this is true.

00:07:48.975 --> 00:07:50.501
Because right now, I tell you this,

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.035
but you're probably saying,
yes, this sounds nice.

00:07:53.035 --> 00:07:55.360
And sure, it could probably work

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.546
for many problems in my life.

00:07:57.546 --> 00:08:00.342
I can see that somehow
I'm catastrophizing them,

00:08:00.342 --> 00:08:02.824
exaggerating them, a lot of
times they don't come true,

00:08:02.824 --> 00:08:05.739
but, you know, there's
just this one problem

00:08:05.739 --> 00:08:07.639
I've got right now, I've
got this one problem

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:09.472
that's just pure hell.

00:08:10.646 --> 00:08:12.898
It's pure hell. It's pure evil.

00:08:12.898 --> 00:08:14.734
There's no possible way that this problem

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:17.184
I've got right here, there's
no possible way that this

00:08:17.184 --> 00:08:20.025
could have any opportunity in it.

00:08:20.025 --> 00:08:21.564
There's no opportunity here.

00:08:21.564 --> 00:08:23.642
There's no lesson to be learned here.

00:08:23.642 --> 00:08:26.136
There's nothing positive,
this is just pure negative.

00:08:26.136 --> 00:08:29.296
If I could remove it from my
life, my life would be happy.

00:08:29.296 --> 00:08:32.416
I would be better, I just know it.

00:08:32.416 --> 00:08:35.000
Well that's exactly what
I'm trying to tell you,

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.665
is that, that's not positive thinking.

00:08:38.665 --> 00:08:41.055
And I understand where you're coming from.

00:08:41.055 --> 00:08:43.348
A lot of times, I get
triggered like that too.

00:08:43.348 --> 00:08:46.925
And I was especially like
that a lot in the past.

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:49.921
And I'm still a bit like that today.

00:08:49.921 --> 00:08:51.744
But you've got to understand
that this is the mode

00:08:51.744 --> 00:08:53.889
of thinking that you've been coming from

00:08:53.889 --> 00:08:57.818
for most of your life,
and that mode of thinking

00:08:57.818 --> 00:09:01.248
has gotten you to where you
are right now in your life.

00:09:01.248 --> 00:09:04.269
So that's gotten you to where you are,

00:09:04.269 --> 00:09:08.019
but, that's only gotten
you to where you are.

00:09:09.412 --> 00:09:11.315
And I'm willing to bet
that you can do better

00:09:11.315 --> 00:09:13.295
than where you are right now.

00:09:13.295 --> 00:09:16.066
And if you really want
to go to that next level,

00:09:16.066 --> 00:09:18.119
then what you have to do, is
you have to start to think

00:09:18.119 --> 00:09:19.831
in a different way.

00:09:19.831 --> 00:09:21.155
Sometimes you have to start thinking

00:09:21.155 --> 00:09:22.922
in a radically different way.

00:09:22.922 --> 00:09:24.745
A way that seems uncomfortable.

00:09:24.745 --> 00:09:28.820
A way that seems wishful
thinking at first.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:32.783
A way that seems unrealistic,
that seems idealistic,

00:09:32.783 --> 00:09:34.700
that seems fantastical.

00:09:37.763 --> 00:09:38.596
Yet,

00:09:40.468 --> 00:09:42.930
there's something to this idea.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.026
That nothing can happen to
you that is not positive.

00:09:46.026 --> 00:09:48.492
I guarantee you that, if
you really look at it,

00:09:48.492 --> 00:09:50.615
if I really sat down
with you to really look

00:09:50.615 --> 00:09:51.812
at that challenge that you have right now

00:09:51.812 --> 00:09:54.312
that's totally unsolvable,
that's ruining your life,

00:09:54.312 --> 00:09:56.402
if we looked at it, we can pick out,

00:09:56.402 --> 00:09:58.317
I guarantee we can pick
out something positive.

00:09:58.317 --> 00:10:00.058
Something that you can learn from it.

00:10:00.058 --> 00:10:01.646
Of course this doesn't
mean that all of a sudden

00:10:01.646 --> 00:10:02.937
your problems will be fixed.

00:10:02.937 --> 00:10:04.717
It doesn't mean that your
problem is not a real problem.

00:10:04.717 --> 00:10:07.822
It doesn't mean that you shouldn't
work to fix your problem.

00:10:07.822 --> 00:10:09.739
It doesn't mean that
you don't feel the pains

00:10:09.739 --> 00:10:11.316
of your problem.

00:10:11.316 --> 00:10:13.965
I'm not denying you any of that.

00:10:13.965 --> 00:10:17.837
But I am saying that, once
you adopt this mindset,

00:10:17.837 --> 00:10:20.117
and you become a positive thinker,

00:10:20.117 --> 00:10:23.897
then you're going to be able to
Akido a lot of your problems.

00:10:23.897 --> 00:10:26.473
If you don't like yourself, then,

00:10:26.473 --> 00:10:27.797
ask yourself the following question.

00:10:27.797 --> 00:10:30.793
Do you really not like yourself?

00:10:30.793 --> 00:10:34.210
Or do you not like an aspect of yourself?

00:10:36.343 --> 00:10:38.706
Big difference, right?

00:10:38.706 --> 00:10:42.835
Is it all of you that you
don't like, or just an aspect?

00:10:42.835 --> 00:10:45.073
I bet it's just an aspect.

00:10:45.073 --> 00:10:47.801
So, if that's the case, first of all,

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:51.864
realize how much you're focusing on it.

00:10:51.864 --> 00:10:53.269
Right?

00:10:53.269 --> 00:10:55.939
And I want you take that
camera that you have right now,

00:10:55.939 --> 00:10:58.164
and you're totally zoomed
in on that one imperfection

00:10:58.164 --> 00:10:59.623
that you had, you're
totally zoomed in on it,

00:10:59.623 --> 00:11:02.051
I want you to zoom out and see yourself

00:11:02.051 --> 00:11:04.387
and your whole life, and the
whole history that you've had

00:11:04.387 --> 00:11:06.576
of your life, and where you're going.

00:11:06.576 --> 00:11:10.743
See all of that, and put that
imperfection into context.

00:11:12.379 --> 00:11:13.212
Right?

00:11:13.212 --> 00:11:15.969
It's still there, I'm not
denying it might not be there.

00:11:15.969 --> 00:11:18.910
Maybe you have some crooked
teeth, or you have a big nose,

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.151
or you have a fat ass, or whatever.

00:11:22.151 --> 00:11:25.645
Or maybe you have some
character flaws in you.

00:11:25.645 --> 00:11:27.779
Not physical problems,
but character flaws,

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:29.330
and you don't like
yourself for those reasons.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.462
Okay, let's admit that that's there.

00:11:31.462 --> 00:11:34.014
Let's say that it's true, it's there.

00:11:34.014 --> 00:11:38.390
Well, that's one aspect
of a much bigger picture.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.579
So, first of all, realize
that that's the case.

00:11:40.579 --> 00:11:44.037
And if that is the case,
then also realize this point.

00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:46.427
You have a choice of what you focus on.

00:11:46.427 --> 00:11:50.097
You've got this laser beam in your mind,

00:11:50.097 --> 00:11:51.906
which is your focus,
right, your awareness.

00:11:51.906 --> 00:11:55.034
And this laser beam, it's
consciously guided by you.

00:11:55.034 --> 00:11:57.449
Not all the time, but you can guide it.

00:11:57.449 --> 00:12:00.587
And so, if you're always
hating on yourself,

00:12:00.587 --> 00:12:02.296
then what you're doing is
you're taking your imperfections

00:12:02.296 --> 00:12:05.599
and you're always shining
a magnifying glass over it.

00:12:05.599 --> 00:12:06.543
So that's what's happening.

00:12:06.543 --> 00:12:08.806
You're shining this magnifying
glass on your imperfections.

00:12:08.806 --> 00:12:12.610
Sometimes, all you do is you
just stare at them all day.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:13.775
Right?

00:12:13.775 --> 00:12:15.698
And that's why you feel so
bad about yourself sometimes,

00:12:15.698 --> 00:12:18.883
because you stare at those
imperfections ceaselessly.

00:12:18.883 --> 00:12:21.689
Well, if you've got an imperfection,

00:12:21.689 --> 00:12:23.589
you only got two choices.

00:12:23.589 --> 00:12:26.741
Either you're going to
fix it, you can change it,

00:12:26.741 --> 00:12:28.490
or you can't.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.204
Now, go out there and try
to change it if you can.

00:12:31.204 --> 00:12:32.649
I mean, that's what I'm all about.

00:12:32.649 --> 00:12:34.932
I'm giving you a lot of advice
and stuff in all my videos

00:12:34.932 --> 00:12:37.119
about how to put your life into place,

00:12:37.119 --> 00:12:38.664
and actually make it really good.

00:12:38.664 --> 00:12:40.194
Objectively good.

00:12:40.194 --> 00:12:41.452
But if you can't change it,

00:12:41.452 --> 00:12:42.718
maybe like your physical appearance,

00:12:42.718 --> 00:12:44.030
you feel like you can't change

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.905
or you don't really want to go that far,

00:12:45.905 --> 00:12:47.305
then that's fine.

00:12:47.305 --> 00:12:49.111
You can learn to accept it, in the sense

00:12:49.111 --> 00:12:51.442
that you're going to
shift your focus away.

00:12:51.442 --> 00:12:54.061
You're going to kind of accept
it, and not look at it anymore.

00:12:54.061 --> 00:12:56.816
Stop looking at it, because
it's the constant looking

00:12:56.816 --> 00:12:58.456
at it and the re-looking
and the re-looking

00:12:58.456 --> 00:13:02.357
and the re-looking that
is really killing you.

00:13:02.357 --> 00:13:04.290
You're going to start to focus
on other areas of your life

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:06.034
that are great, and what
you're going to realize,

00:13:06.034 --> 00:13:07.990
when you make that shift, is
you're going to realize that,

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.491
well, that little imperfection,

00:13:09.491 --> 00:13:11.566
it's not that important anymore.

00:13:11.566 --> 00:13:13.270
And then maybe a couple
years down the road

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.281
you will actually laugh.

00:13:15.281 --> 00:13:17.738
You will laugh, because
you'll laugh and say,

00:13:17.738 --> 00:13:21.393
how could I have possibly
been so concerned about that?

00:13:21.393 --> 00:13:23.136
It's so insignificant now
because I've got all this other

00:13:23.136 --> 00:13:25.835
awesome stuff flourishing in my life.

00:13:25.835 --> 00:13:28.386
Next point: do not quit.

00:13:28.386 --> 00:13:31.969
Successful people are
extremely persistent.

00:13:33.124 --> 00:13:35.796
We do not quit when it gets tough.

00:13:35.796 --> 00:13:37.441
And it will get tough.

00:13:37.441 --> 00:13:39.630
I don't care how passionate you
are about what you're doing.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:40.953
I don't care how much you love it,

00:13:40.953 --> 00:13:42.465
or you love it or you don't.

00:13:42.465 --> 00:13:44.194
There's going to be ups and downs in life,

00:13:44.194 --> 00:13:46.431
and whatever you're pursuing,
whatever kind of big goal

00:13:46.431 --> 00:13:48.779
you set for yourself, especially
if you set those big goals,

00:13:48.779 --> 00:13:50.265
they're going to be challenging.

00:13:50.265 --> 00:13:52.061
They're going to require you to grow.

00:13:52.061 --> 00:13:53.248
They're going to require you to step

00:13:53.248 --> 00:13:55.679
outside your comfort zone,
and that means emotional labor

00:13:55.679 --> 00:13:57.175
will be involved.

00:13:57.175 --> 00:14:01.765
That's okay, but, to make sure
that you get through that,

00:14:01.765 --> 00:14:04.601
and to get to your ultimate
objective of success,

00:14:04.601 --> 00:14:07.515
you're going to have to have persistent,

00:14:07.515 --> 00:14:10.199
and you can't quit when
the going gets tough.

00:14:10.199 --> 00:14:12.064
So, maybe you're working on a project

00:14:12.064 --> 00:14:14.573
and something's not working
out the way you want.

00:14:14.573 --> 00:14:16.477
Something slips, something fails,

00:14:16.477 --> 00:14:19.270
and you're really tempted to
quit and throw in the towel.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:21.030
Or maybe there's a relationship,

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.484
and you're trying to work it out,

00:14:23.484 --> 00:14:25.757
but it's not working, and
you're tempted to drop it.

00:14:25.757 --> 00:14:27.100
You're tempted to quit there.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:31.839
Whatever part of your life
you really want to quit,

00:14:31.839 --> 00:14:34.621
or drop right now, if you're
in that kind of point,

00:14:34.621 --> 00:14:36.656
you got to push through it

00:14:36.656 --> 00:14:39.045
if it's really aligned with your values

00:14:39.045 --> 00:14:40.409
and aligned with your purpose.

00:14:40.409 --> 00:14:42.229
If it's not aligned, you can drop it.

00:14:42.229 --> 00:14:43.568
In fact, you should.

00:14:43.568 --> 00:14:46.398
But otherwise, you have to
be very, very persistent.

00:14:46.398 --> 00:14:50.300
If you read biographies of
the most successful people

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.878
throughout human history,
business leaders,

00:14:52.878 --> 00:14:56.619
social leaders, politicians,
celebrities, actors,

00:14:56.619 --> 00:15:00.584
you know that just the underlying theme

00:15:00.584 --> 00:15:04.417
of all those biographies
and all the histories

00:15:05.336 --> 00:15:07.535
is that they were very, very persistent.

00:15:07.535 --> 00:15:09.262
They were okay with failure.

00:15:09.262 --> 00:15:11.636
In fact, most of these people,
they were so successful

00:15:11.636 --> 00:15:14.756
because they failed so much,
that they just couldn't,

00:15:14.756 --> 00:15:16.875
their success was inevitable,
because after you fail

00:15:16.875 --> 00:15:20.735
thousands of times, you
start to learn your lessons,

00:15:20.735 --> 00:15:21.934
and you start to get good,

00:15:21.934 --> 00:15:25.095
and the human brain is really,
really, really stubborn,

00:15:25.095 --> 00:15:26.770
and it doesn't tend to learn from success

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:28.456
as much as it does from failure.

00:15:28.456 --> 00:15:31.155
So, when you're failing a
lot, don't get discouraged.

00:15:31.155 --> 00:15:32.738
Push on. Persevere.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.703
Go through your hardest moments,

00:15:36.703 --> 00:15:38.835
because those hardest
moments that you go through,

00:15:38.835 --> 00:15:40.577
that's when you learn
your biggest lessons,

00:15:40.577 --> 00:15:43.277
and those are what grow
you to be able to handle

00:15:43.277 --> 00:15:44.707
bigger and bigger challenges.

00:15:44.707 --> 00:15:47.015
To accomplish more and more,
and get the kind of success

00:15:47.015 --> 00:15:48.580
that you want.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.875
And these are also, coincidentally,

00:15:50.875 --> 00:15:52.791
the proudest moments of your life.

00:15:52.791 --> 00:15:56.030
The moments of your life that
you will never, ever regret.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.986
So never quit when you're doing something

00:15:57.986 --> 00:16:00.218
that's important to you.

00:16:00.218 --> 00:16:03.954
Being able to focus is
critical to getting the results

00:16:03.954 --> 00:16:05.047
that you want.

00:16:05.047 --> 00:16:08.714
Focus is all about
eliminating distractions.

00:16:10.367 --> 00:16:12.456
So, what are the distractions right now

00:16:12.456 --> 00:16:14.791
that are keeping you from being focused?

00:16:14.791 --> 00:16:16.972
Go ahead and sit down, pause this video,

00:16:16.972 --> 00:16:18.922
and jot down five things.

00:16:18.922 --> 00:16:20.455
What are five things that
are keeping you distracted

00:16:20.455 --> 00:16:22.999
in whatever area of life
you want more focus in.

00:16:22.999 --> 00:16:25.009
So, are you not focused at work?

00:16:25.009 --> 00:16:26.510
What is distracting you?

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.593
Is it hunger?

00:16:28.558 --> 00:16:30.493
Because you're not eating in the morning?

00:16:30.493 --> 00:16:32.973
Is it your boss who comes in,

00:16:32.973 --> 00:16:35.199
and disturbs you every 15 minutes?

00:16:35.199 --> 00:16:36.282
Is it emails?

00:16:37.143 --> 00:16:39.382
Is it the Twitter feed that's pinging you?

00:16:39.382 --> 00:16:42.067
Is it your cellphone
that's vibrating from texts

00:16:42.067 --> 00:16:44.081
that you're getting hit up with?

00:16:44.081 --> 00:16:46.846
What is distracting you?

00:16:46.846 --> 00:16:49.480
What about at school, what's
distracting you there?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.694
What about your relationship,
what's distracting you there?

00:16:51.694 --> 00:16:53.842
Sit down and identify those factors.

00:16:53.842 --> 00:16:55.433
'Cause once you've got those identified,

00:16:55.433 --> 00:16:57.592
I think what you'll find is actually that,

00:16:57.592 --> 00:16:59.934
one of the biggest
factors that you'll find,

00:16:59.934 --> 00:17:01.763
is multi-tasking.

00:17:01.763 --> 00:17:04.760
You trying to do multiple
things at one time.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:07.269
And that, of course, is
the antithesis of focus.

00:17:07.269 --> 00:17:08.969
When you're doing multiple things,

00:17:08.969 --> 00:17:10.806
you're not focused by definition.

00:17:10.806 --> 00:17:13.013
You're splitting your focus,
and when you split your focus,

00:17:13.013 --> 00:17:15.828
it's like, you know what it's like,

00:17:15.828 --> 00:17:18.675
imagine if we had the sun.

00:17:18.675 --> 00:17:21.355
It was a bright sunny day, and
I gave you a magnifying glass

00:17:21.355 --> 00:17:23.603
and I said, here, you can
take this magnifying glass,

00:17:23.603 --> 00:17:26.530
and if you hold it up at the right angle

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:27.949
and you hold it steady,

00:17:27.949 --> 00:17:31.093
then you can burn that ant
right there on the ground.

00:17:31.093 --> 00:17:33.467
Or you can set that leaf on fire.

00:17:33.467 --> 00:17:36.776
And, first thought, you'd say,
wow, if you didn't know that,

00:17:36.776 --> 00:17:38.662
you'd say, wow, that's amazing,
I can't believe that's true.

00:17:38.662 --> 00:17:39.741
Let me try it.

00:17:39.741 --> 00:17:41.945
Then you take that magnifying
glass and you'd run over,

00:17:41.945 --> 00:17:46.112
and you try to burn an ant
or burn a piece of leaf.

00:17:47.156 --> 00:17:49.883
But of course, if you
didn't listen to the fact

00:17:49.883 --> 00:17:53.349
that I told you, that you
have to keep it steady,

00:17:53.349 --> 00:17:55.752
and you have to focus the rays,

00:17:55.752 --> 00:17:56.642
then what's going to happen, is,

00:17:56.642 --> 00:17:59.465
you're going to just kind of
move it around, move it around,

00:17:59.465 --> 00:18:02.454
move it around, and you're
going to come back to me,

00:18:02.454 --> 00:18:03.635
and you're going to say, what the hell?

00:18:03.635 --> 00:18:05.269
Nothing worked. You're lying to me.

00:18:05.269 --> 00:18:06.172
This doesn't work.

00:18:06.172 --> 00:18:08.398
It's not possible to take the sun's rays

00:18:08.398 --> 00:18:09.561
and burn anything with them.

00:18:09.561 --> 00:18:11.443
They're too weak.

00:18:11.443 --> 00:18:12.757
And of course, the
problem is that you didn't

00:18:12.757 --> 00:18:14.500
focus the rays first.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.010
That's exactly what
it's like in your life.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.998
If you're trying to get some success

00:18:18.998 --> 00:18:21.060
in your career, in your business,

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:23.853
at school, what you need to do,

00:18:23.853 --> 00:18:27.278
is you need to put your
full attention on it.

00:18:27.278 --> 00:18:29.902
You need to bring all
those rays to a point.

00:18:29.902 --> 00:18:31.628
You need to bring your
thoughts to a point.

00:18:31.628 --> 00:18:33.533
Your mind has to be
focused on whatever it is

00:18:33.533 --> 00:18:34.366
that you're doing.

00:18:34.366 --> 00:18:36.440
Of all the things that I regret the most,

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.341
is I regret that I didn't start meditating

00:18:38.341 --> 00:18:41.460
when I was six or seven years old.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:44.444
If I started that habit, man,

00:18:44.444 --> 00:18:47.546
I would be at such a different
place in my life right now.

00:18:47.546 --> 00:18:50.922
I'd be so much happier.
So much more fulfilled.

00:18:50.922 --> 00:18:54.672
Meditation is the key
to mastering happiness.

00:18:56.133 --> 00:18:58.211
And happiness is different than success.

00:18:58.211 --> 00:19:00.316
You could read all the self
help books in the world

00:19:00.316 --> 00:19:02.907
and become very successful,
but you still will not be

00:19:02.907 --> 00:19:04.355
fulfilled and happy.

00:19:04.355 --> 00:19:06.757
And that's because you
haven't practiced meditation.

00:19:06.757 --> 00:19:08.340
So, start tomorrow.

00:19:10.563 --> 00:19:13.263
20 minutes a day at the very least.

00:19:13.263 --> 00:19:15.947
Make that commitment for
the rest of your life.

00:19:15.947 --> 00:19:18.043
You're going to meditate
for 20 minutes every day

00:19:18.043 --> 00:19:20.314
for the rest of your life, no matter what.

00:19:20.314 --> 00:19:23.872
No sick days, no days off,
you're never going to miss a day.

00:19:23.872 --> 00:19:27.003
Starting tomorrow, that's your mission.

00:19:27.003 --> 00:19:29.099
And then, after a year or two,

00:19:29.099 --> 00:19:31.589
I recommend that you bump
that up to one hour per day,

00:19:31.589 --> 00:19:33.402
if you really want to supercharge

00:19:33.402 --> 00:19:35.913
your fulfillment levels in life

00:19:35.913 --> 00:19:38.817
And then the last point, and
this is one of my favorites,

00:19:38.817 --> 00:19:40.855
and this is one that
people really miss out on,

00:19:40.855 --> 00:19:42.272
is study success.

00:19:43.794 --> 00:19:46.804
Successful people study success.

00:19:46.804 --> 00:19:49.166
Success is not what we naively think,

00:19:49.166 --> 00:19:52.756
just something that happens
naturally to some people,

00:19:52.756 --> 00:19:54.315
and doesn't happen to other people.

00:19:54.315 --> 00:19:57.034
Success is a very deliberate,
conscious endeavor

00:19:57.034 --> 00:19:57.977
that you undertake.

00:19:57.977 --> 00:20:00.962
Success is built over months and years,

00:20:00.962 --> 00:20:02.637
and it's done consciously.

00:20:02.637 --> 00:20:05.672
And the more you understand
the principles of success,

00:20:05.672 --> 00:20:07.643
the concepts of success,

00:20:07.643 --> 00:20:10.018
the more you study people
who have been successful,

00:20:10.018 --> 00:20:12.394
the more you see what it really takes.

00:20:12.394 --> 00:20:14.418
And that process of
success, those principles,

00:20:14.418 --> 00:20:16.154
are not always what they seem.

00:20:16.154 --> 00:20:18.359
And to me, this is something
that I've really committed

00:20:18.359 --> 00:20:19.912
my life to, is studying these principles.

00:20:19.912 --> 00:20:22.290
I really love it. It's exciting for me.

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.110
I really encourage you to
get involved with that.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.429
So that means, maybe,
attending some seminars.

00:20:26.429 --> 00:20:29.321
Reading some books, watching these videos,

00:20:29.321 --> 00:20:32.100
learning about it, maybe
joining a group of friends

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.293
that are successful,
joining a mastermind group.

00:20:35.293 --> 00:20:36.891
Be around successful people,

00:20:36.891 --> 00:20:39.225
learn how the success process works,

00:20:39.225 --> 00:20:41.577
and learn the psychology of success.

00:20:41.577 --> 00:20:44.450
Not the externals of
success, but the psychology.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:45.577
That's what we're talking about.

