00:22:24.335 --> 00:22:26.915
So make a list of all these different ways

00:22:26.915 --> 00:22:29.437
that you are not being confident.

00:22:29.437 --> 00:22:31.596
Then what I want you to do, is I want you

00:22:31.596 --> 00:22:34.510
to analyze each one of those
situations that you're facing

00:22:34.510 --> 00:22:37.254
and say, what is an
alternative set of actions

00:22:37.254 --> 00:22:39.088
that you could be taking?

00:22:39.088 --> 00:22:41.431
So, what would a
confident person be doing?

00:22:41.431 --> 00:22:44.609
So, let's say, in that date situation,

00:22:44.609 --> 00:22:46.605
what would the most confident person,

00:22:46.605 --> 00:22:48.780
who's extremely confident
with the opposite sex,

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:51.386
what would he or she do?

00:22:51.386 --> 00:22:52.979
How would he or she think?

00:22:52.979 --> 00:22:55.002
And jot down some specific points.

00:22:55.002 --> 00:22:57.361
How would he talk about his stories?

00:22:57.361 --> 00:23:00.901
How would she be thinking
about the situation?

00:23:00.901 --> 00:23:03.559
How would he or she be
carrying themselves,

00:23:03.559 --> 00:23:04.746
what would the body language be like,

00:23:04.746 --> 00:23:06.096
what would the thought process be?

00:23:06.096 --> 00:23:08.972
Same thing with the situation
at work or anywhere else.

00:23:08.972 --> 00:23:12.644
Make a list of alternative
actions that you could be taking

00:23:12.644 --> 00:23:16.963
that would feel confident
to you if you took them.

00:23:16.963 --> 00:23:19.662
So, that is going to be your game plan.

00:23:19.662 --> 00:23:21.051
Once you identify the situations,

00:23:21.051 --> 00:23:22.779
and you identify the alternative actions,

00:23:22.779 --> 00:23:25.107
you kind of know what you need to do.

00:23:25.107 --> 00:23:26.411
Basically, what you need to do,

00:23:26.411 --> 00:23:28.057
is you need to start
changing your behaviors,

00:23:28.057 --> 00:23:30.824
and you need to start now living in,

00:23:30.824 --> 00:23:33.807
and practicing, those alternative actions.

00:23:33.807 --> 00:23:37.535
You have to have a deep
understanding of who you really are

00:23:37.535 --> 00:23:41.770
in life to have long
term sustainable success,

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:44.194
and both happiness and
then fulfillment, right?

00:23:44.194 --> 00:23:46.955
And for me, success is
shallow if it doesn't come

00:23:46.955 --> 00:23:49.357
with the happiness and
fulfillment component.

00:23:49.357 --> 00:23:51.450
So for me, I want to get all of it.

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:53.778
Both the external success
and then the fulfillment,

00:23:53.778 --> 00:23:57.193
the lasting fulfillment and
happiness that you can get

00:23:57.193 --> 00:23:58.026
with that.

00:23:58.026 --> 00:24:00.253
I don't want just
shallow external success.

00:24:00.253 --> 00:24:01.969
And to do that, you need
to really understand

00:24:01.969 --> 00:24:03.694
and discover who you are.

00:24:03.694 --> 00:24:05.695
And you might be thinking,
well, I know who I am.

00:24:05.695 --> 00:24:07.462
No. You don't.

00:24:07.462 --> 00:24:10.161
Most people out there,
I'd say 99% of people

00:24:10.161 --> 00:24:11.822
do not really know who they are,

00:24:11.822 --> 00:24:14.129
because they have not gone
on the journey that it takes

00:24:14.129 --> 00:24:15.697
to discover that.

00:24:15.697 --> 00:24:17.078
And what I'm really talking about here,

00:24:17.078 --> 00:24:18.556
this is not some abstract notion,

00:24:18.556 --> 00:24:21.458
is you're going to discover
what your top ten values are.

00:24:21.458 --> 00:24:23.457
You need to discover what
your top five feelings

00:24:23.457 --> 00:24:24.986
are in life.

00:24:24.986 --> 00:24:26.897
You need to discover what
it is that you really want

00:24:26.897 --> 00:24:29.443
out of life, what is meaningful to you.

00:24:29.443 --> 00:24:32.744
And you've got to also
discover what you don't want.

00:24:32.744 --> 00:24:34.903
And you might say, well,
I know what I don't want.

00:24:34.903 --> 00:24:36.319
I know the things I don't like.

00:24:36.319 --> 00:24:38.370
Well, there might not
be as much clarity there

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:40.234
as you think there is.

00:24:40.234 --> 00:24:41.554
So this is all about the matter

00:24:41.554 --> 00:24:43.998
of clarity and articulation.

00:24:43.998 --> 00:24:45.659
It's one thing to know vaguely.

00:24:45.659 --> 00:24:48.104
It's a totally different thing
to actually articulate it.

00:24:48.104 --> 00:24:52.233
Write it down, and note
very, very consciously.

00:24:52.233 --> 00:24:54.294
It's going to clear a
lot of things up for you,

00:24:54.294 --> 00:24:57.551
and if you sit down and do this process,

00:24:57.551 --> 00:24:59.737
you're going to quickly realize
that you don't know as much

00:24:59.737 --> 00:25:01.707
about yourself as you think you do.

00:25:01.707 --> 00:25:04.585
And you probably have
had moments in your life

00:25:04.585 --> 00:25:06.284
that have been like epiphanies,

00:25:06.284 --> 00:25:08.293
where you had deep self-discovery,

00:25:08.293 --> 00:25:10.156
whether it was when you
were traveling, maybe it was

00:25:10.156 --> 00:25:12.626
after a break up in a relationship.

00:25:12.626 --> 00:25:15.423
Maybe it was when you
were struggling at work.

00:25:15.423 --> 00:25:17.256
You discovered things about yourself,

00:25:17.256 --> 00:25:21.051
and by going through these
challenging experiences,

00:25:21.051 --> 00:25:23.345
we really discover what it
is that we want out of life.

00:25:23.345 --> 00:25:25.556
And that's the foundation.

00:25:25.556 --> 00:25:27.864
Successful people know what they want.

00:25:27.864 --> 00:25:31.718
I want you to read one self-help
book every single month.

00:25:31.718 --> 00:25:33.147
It's not a lot, just one per month,

00:25:33.147 --> 00:25:34.617
that's not a lot, you can handle that.

00:25:34.617 --> 00:25:37.536
Most self-help books are pretty short.

00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:39.965
So, all you need to do
is just have a list,

00:25:39.965 --> 00:25:42.789
and in fact I have a list
of some of my favorite,

00:25:42.789 --> 00:25:45.041
most powerful self-help
books on my website,

00:25:45.041 --> 00:25:47.093
you can go check that
out at Actualized.org.

00:25:47.093 --> 00:25:50.853
But this is a huge habit. Here's why.

00:25:50.853 --> 00:25:54.349
Because self-help books
have basically distilled

00:25:54.349 --> 00:25:57.492
all the principles of
success and happiness

00:25:57.492 --> 00:26:01.612
that human beings have
discovered in the last,

00:26:01.612 --> 00:26:02.612
2,000 years.

00:26:03.559 --> 00:26:04.995
And especially the last hundred years,

00:26:04.995 --> 00:26:06.604
there's been so much research done

00:26:06.604 --> 00:26:08.751
on how to be successful in business,

00:26:08.751 --> 00:26:10.286
how to be successful in relationships,

00:26:10.286 --> 00:26:12.448
how to be successful with
your happiness levels,

00:26:12.448 --> 00:26:14.864
how to meditate properly,
the scientific benefits

00:26:14.864 --> 00:26:18.399
of meditation, and so on and so forth.

00:26:18.399 --> 00:26:22.138
And self-help books are not just abstract,

00:26:22.138 --> 00:26:25.716
very pedantic types of books
that you might read in college.

00:26:25.716 --> 00:26:27.821
These are very practical.

00:26:27.821 --> 00:26:29.669
These are written to get you results.

00:26:29.669 --> 00:26:31.913
These self-books have exercises in them.

00:26:31.913 --> 00:26:33.612
They have techniques.

00:26:33.612 --> 00:26:36.529
Read those, start practicing those.

00:26:38.469 --> 00:26:41.965
If you just read one book per month,

00:26:41.965 --> 00:26:44.559
for the next, let's say eight years,

00:26:44.559 --> 00:26:47.662
that would be close to a hundred books.

00:26:47.662 --> 00:26:50.428
That would give you the
entire theoretical foundation

00:26:50.428 --> 00:26:52.845
that you need to master life.

00:26:54.196 --> 00:26:55.083
(whooshing sound)

